{"created": "2026-08-13T19:55:33.344803+00:00", "modified": "2026-08-13T19:55:33.698480+00:00", "id": 21924442, "conceptrecid": "19615974", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21924442", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.19615974", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21924442", "metadata": {"title": "Global habitat suitability dataset for Aedes aegypti and Aedes albopictus derived using the Climademic Suitability Model", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21924442", "publication_date": "2026-08-13", "description": "<p>This dataset includes modelled habitat suitability probabilities for the mosquito species Aedes aegypti and Aedes albopictus based on the Climademic Suitability Model. The data provide monthly estimates of environmental suitability across the globe over multiple decades from 1975 to 2024.<br>All details describing the used feature data sets, model implementation and analysis, and suitability discussion are presented in the accompanying manuscript &ldquo;Global monthly habitat suitability for Aedes<br>vectors in 1975&ndash;2024&rdquo; by Siddiqui et al.</p>\n<p>This work is funded by the German Federal Ministry of Research, Technology and Space (BMFTR) through the CLIMADEMIC project (funding code 01LN2210A) within the framework of the Research for Sustainability Strategy (FONA), and by the German Federal Ministry of Health (BMG) through the AI-DAVis-PANDEMICS project (funding code 2523DAT400).</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Siddiqui, Tarique Adnan", "affiliation": "Leibniz-Institute of Atmospheric Physics", "orcid": "0000-0001-9394-6708"}, {"name": "Malysheva, Nadezhda", "affiliation": "Robert Koch Institute", "orcid": "0000-0001-7825-0067"}, {"name": "Hartner, Anna-Maria", "affiliation": "Robert Koch Institute", "orcid": "0000-0002-8502-9915"}, {"name": "Parreira, Diogo", "affiliation": "Robert Koch Institute", "orcid": "0009-0004-3685-6801"}, {"name": "Genger, Jakob-Wendelin", "affiliation": "Robert Koch Institute", "orcid": "0000-0003-4502-1094"}, {"